   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Soile, thank you so much for your message - and I&#39;m sorry for the delay! This is a good question. It should be output by the estimate_profiles() function. If you save that output to an object, i.e., my_output (e.g., my_output &lt;- estimate_profiles(d, V1, V2, V3, n_profiles = 3)), you should be able to use my_output as a data frame with the observations and the cases.<div><br></div><div>Note that the development version of tidyLPA includes a helper function, get_data(), which will return this, i.e. get_data(my_output). </div><div><br></div><div>Do be in touch with any questions - we&#39;ll try to respond much more promptly next time.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Josh </div></div>"
    ],
